   {
    "heading": "Eight good Twitch names",
    "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, two from each style:</p><ul><li><strong>CopperOtterTV</strong>: a channel brand. The TV on the end tells people it's a channel, not just a player.</li><li><strong>TheWanderingHeron</strong>: a brand that suits a variety streamer who plays a bit of everything.</li><li><strong>PebblePlays</strong>: chat-friendly, short enough that viewers can @ you without a typo.</li><li><strong>ItsMochi</strong>: the greeting style many streamers use, so the name reads like a hello.</li><li><strong>MossAndMilk</strong>: cosy and gentle, for slow games, crafts or late-night chatting.</li><li><strong>SleepyFernCorner</strong>: cosy, with a place word that makes the channel sound like somewhere to sit.</li><li><strong>RubbishAtParking</strong>: funny, and it gives chat something to tease you about.</li><li><strong>GooseWithAHeadset</strong>: a silly picture that people remember after one stream.</li></ul>"
